{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"No independent grouped-GEMM API is available without copying multi-gigabyte weights. The viable low-risk optimization is layout-based: one reusable contiguous workspace, `out=` GEMMs, in-place buffer reuse after each dependency dies, and one strided-batched call for the two weight gradients that share `x`. This preserves the exact GEMM algorithms while reducing nine allocations to one and six GEMM submissions to five."}}
